%% Figure 7 — Custodial-to-Sovereign Wallet Migration Protocol
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant RF as Refugee Portal
    participant AW as Aid Worker<br/>Wallet Migration Tools
    participant PW as Pera Wallet W2
    participant API as FastAPI
    participant JSON as migration-requests.json
    participant AD as Admin Portal
    participant SC as RefugeeContract

    RF->>API: POST /api/blockchain/migration-request-lite<br/>{ identity_id }
    API->>JSON: PENDING (no W2 yet)
    API-->>RF: Request submitted

    AW->>API: GET /api/blockchain/migration-message
    API-->>AW: challenge nonce + message
    AW->>PW: signData(message)
    PW-->>AW: signature σ
    AW->>API: POST /api/blockchain/migration-request<br/>{ identity_id, newWallet, signature }
    API->>API: verify_bytes(σ, message, W2)
    API->>JSON: PENDING with W2 + signature

    AD->>API: POST /api/blockchain/migration-approve
    API->>SC: migrate_wallet(W1, W2)<br/>if W2 opted in
    SC->>SC: Copy local state W1 → W2<br/>W1.identity_hash = MIGRATED
    API->>JSON: APPROVED + on_chain_result
    API-->>AD: Migration complete
